# mcp-notes

Notes tools.

An MCP server built with [mcpkit](https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/mcpkit)
on the official MCP Go SDK. It speaks Streamable HTTP (stateless) and stdio.

## Run

```bash
go mod tidy
make run          # HTTP on :8080, endpoint /mcp
make run-stdio    # stdio, for desktop clients and the MCP Inspector
make test
```

## Configuration

| Variable | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `MCP_TRANSPORT` | `http` | `http` or `stdio` |
| `MCP_ADDR` | `:8080` | HTTP listen address |
| `MCP_RESOURCE_URL` | | Public URL of `/mcp`; setting it requires a bearer token on every request |
| `MCP_AUTH_SERVERS` | | Comma-separated authorization server (issuer) URLs advertised in the protected-resource metadata |
| `MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | | Comma-separated browser origins allowed to call the server (CORS) |
| `MCP_TOOL_TIMEOUT` | `2m` | Deadline for each tool call |
| `MCP_SHUTDOWN_TIMEOUT` | `30s` | Graceful shutdown drain time |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | `info` | `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error` |
| `UPSTREAM_TOKEN` | | Upstream API token in stdio mode |

With auth enabled the bearer token is the upstream API's OAuth token and is
passed through to tools (`mcpkit.TokenFrom(ctx)`). To verify tokens from your
own identity provider instead, use `github.com/dungnh3/kitchen/mcpkit/jwtauth`.

## Add a tool

Define typed input and output structs and register a handler in
`internal/tools`. The JSON schema is inferred from the struct tags, input is
validated before your handler runs, and a returned error becomes a tool
result the model can read.
